Interesting — a wrinkle I didn't anticipate: STAMP shows `committed=none` in all fixture runs. Why? My fixtures DO have `reports/round-69/accept-d.py` written. Oh — look at evaluate():

  ```python
  mine = sha256_file(os.path.join(HERE, SELF))
  committed = sha256_file(os.path.join(root, "reports", "round-69", SELF))
  ```

  `SELF = os.path.basename(__file__)`. When I run `/tmp/mutd1/accept-d-orig.py`, `__file__` basename is `accept-d-orig.py`, not `accept-d.py`! So it looks for `reports/round-69/accept-d-orig.py` in the root — not found → committed=none → STAMP fails.

  So my "embed the same counter" plan failed because the embedded file is named `accept-d.py` but SELF is `accept-d-orig.py` etc. Fix: name the runner copies exactly `accept-d.py` inside per-variant directories: /tmp/mutd1/orig/accept-d.py, /tmp/mutd1/mut1/accept-d.py, /tmp/mutd1/mut2/accept-d.py. Then SELF = accept-d.py for all, and the embedded copies match.

  This actually demonstrates another finding: STAMP depends on the basename of the running script — a renamed copy of the counter will always fail STAMP against the lane tree (good tamper evidence for the real lane run, since the lane's committed file is accept-d.py). But for the mutation experiment I want STAMP green to isolate STATES/TABLE. Redo with per-variant dirs.

  Also note [D] gave legs 7/8 with only STAMP failing — confirming my fixture builder produces an equivalent-green fixture to the selftest's own green fixture (which showed 8/8 with STAMP green since build_fixture_root copies the counter as accept-d.py). So after the rename fix, [D] should be 8/8 — matching selftest green. That cross-validates my builder.

  Rerun with the fix. Quick edit to mutdrive.py: change the script paths to <variant>/accept-d.py and adjust SHA print. Let me edit.

